CHAPTER.VERS:
And when they opposed themselves and blasphemed, he shook out his raiment and said to them, Your

          {+}
         blood [be] on your

          {+}
         own heads; I am clean: from now on I will go to the Gentiles.

But when Paul was about to open his mouth, Gallio said to the Jews, If indeed it were a matter of wrong or of wicked villany, O you

          {+}
         Jews, there would be a reason that I should bear with you

          {+}
        :

but if they are questions about words and names and your

          {+}
         own law, look to it yourselves; I am not minded to be a judge of these matters.

but taking his leave of them, and saying, I will return again to you

          {+}
         if God wills, he set sail from Ephesus.
